{"title":"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/6/526715fb9a391a9557276efc30584ee731b08f18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1,p_2,p_3,...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"11\" /> be the prime numbers listed in increasing order, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f1249ad95b7682b8316ad21de8ce4ee9fdcf93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> be a real number between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. For positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, define\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8cf2d0e027bf6ce4aa7ac1ee52966e38b73d548.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{k}=\\begin{cases}0&amp;\\text{ if }x_{k-1}=0\\\\ \\left\\{\\frac{p_{k}}{x_{k-1}}\\right\\}&amp;\\text{ if }x_{k-1}\\ne0\\end{cases}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"220\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3df2919191b1220773d9b0142dec5c3528fd4c42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the fractional part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. (The fractional part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is given by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e0750000dbb8c44345a25e37db9debfc0c4d6f9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-\\lfloor{x}\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"19\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/1/d618c9b39b6f26bd5761aace8dfa1257de0a286e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor{x}\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> is the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.) Find, with proof, all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f1249ad95b7682b8316ad21de8ce4ee9fdcf93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/f/2cf5803872dbc90c625ca74f67515a77ec140b00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x_0&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" /> for which the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/7/b57eab14db6408db514dbf3970d4eefe54658c9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0,x_1,x_2,...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"11\" /> eventually becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>All rational numbers between 0 and 1 inclusive will eventually yield some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/0/2e09a5367676e7425fee60f5945e1be1693b7080.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />. To begin, note that by definition, all rational numbers can be written as a quotient of coprime integers. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83a2fa63aaf831891b35db9c3c6901a5eb64b4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0 = \\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46ba6ed097cc88ded349bf99eea89817f135f470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"11\" /> are coprime positive integers. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/f/2cf5803872dbc90c625ca74f67515a77ec140b00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x_0&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6c71b4348561454f4334e03612da76efda26c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;m&lt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"84\" height=\"13\" />. Now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/b/edb1b4059ddf2b3a88b757672482aae3985e1a3b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_1 = \\left\\{\\frac{p_1}{\\frac{m}{n}}\\right\\}=\\left\\{\\frac{np_1}{m}\\right\\}.\\]\" width=\"175\" height=\"45\" /> From this, we can see that applying the iterative process will decrease the value of the denominator, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/c/3cc5d678e78938bc0ceb0fed5e5694362b69fb36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m&lt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" />. Moreover, the numerator is always smaller than the denominator, thanks to the fractional part operator. So we have a strictly decreasing denominator that bounds the numerator. Thus, the numerator will eventually become 0.\n</p><p>On the other hand, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f1249ad95b7682b8316ad21de8ce4ee9fdcf93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> is irrational, then a simple induction will show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5d3dead9cb8d5f6327c737e014850be7a29d0f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> will always be irrational. Indeed, the base case has been established, and, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5d3dead9cb8d5f6327c737e014850be7a29d0f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> is irrational, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/1/23182fd81be9a31090a3cff7ce37a1a77318d3c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{p_{k+1}}{x_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"36\" height=\"35\" /> must be too, and likewise for its fractional portion, which differs from it by an integer. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/1/191ef26bc72336cc70cc3ebe81e035852ced438a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> is irrational, completing the proof.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO\" title=\"1997 USAMO\">1997 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1997\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017090623\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 180/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1284/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5130/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.627      1 -total\n 56.12%    6.525      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 42.00%    4.883      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9705:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017090623 and revision id 67817. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}